1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:07,343
Meet Cowork Adoption Intelligence: a testing, data-free Power BI template that turns approved Cowork audit exports into a clear adoption story.

2
00:00:07,344 --> 00:00:13,277
See reach, return, delegated work, workflow maturity, potential champions, and modeled value.

3
00:00:13,278 --> 00:00:16,013
Here is a quick tour of the decisions it supports.

4
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:20,713
Start Here routes program owners to the right question: Is adoption growing?

5
00:00:20,714 --> 00:00:22,188
Are people returning?

6
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:24,078
How deeply do they delegate?

7
00:00:24,079 --> 00:00:25,968
Where are potential champions?

8
00:00:25,969 --> 00:00:29,924
Begin with the decision, then follow the report to the right page and evidence.

9
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:33,563
Executive Summary reads the latest active week.

10
00:00:33,564 --> 00:00:35,964
Users and task threads show reach.

11
00:00:35,965 --> 00:00:39,281
Prompts, active days, and return rate show habit.

12
00:00:39,282 --> 00:00:46,239
The momentum score balances return, consistency, intensity, and advanced delegation, so always read it with its components.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,522
Weekly Adoption and Usage shows the latest twelve active weeks.

14
00:00:50,523 --> 00:00:55,020
Switch metrics without clearing filters, and use the heatmap to find concentration.

15
00:00:55,021 --> 00:01:00,453
Compare the same period and population, and check rollout timing or export coverage before calling a trend.

16
00:01:01,208 --> 00:01:07,447
User Maturity combines rolling usage tiers, multi-skill task share, task duration, and the delegation ladder.

17
00:01:07,448 --> 00:01:12,564
These signals can show readiness for advanced workflows, but may also reflect retries or friction.

18
00:01:12,565 --> 00:01:14,936
Pair them with role and work context.

19
00:01:15,708 --> 00:01:19,998
Cowork Champions identifies potential enablement partners, not top performers.

20
00:01:19,999 --> 00:01:23,462
Eligibility requires three threads across two active weeks.

21
00:01:23,463 --> 00:01:29,741
The score combines forty percent activity, thirty-five percent consistency, and twenty-five percent delegation maturity.

22
00:01:29,742 --> 00:01:33,806
Confirm role fit, willingness, and manager support before outreach.

23
00:01:34,575 --> 00:01:40,410
Actions by Category groups observed skills into work patterns and exposes unmapped tools for taxonomy maintenance.

24
00:01:40,411 --> 00:01:44,199
Action value tiers are category references, not user scores.

25
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:48,805
Validate the dominant categories before recommending a new workflow or enablement scenario.

26
00:01:49,551 --> 00:01:55,042
Activity and Value applies selected low, mid, or high time benchmarks to observed task volume.

27
00:01:55,043 --> 00:01:58,584
Estimated value also requires a customer-selected labor rate.

28
00:01:58,585 --> 00:02:04,126
Present a range, keep the assumptions visible, and label every result as modeled, not realized savings.

29
00:02:04,887 --> 00:02:10,329
The Adoption Metric Guide keeps definitions, thresholds, dependencies, and boundaries visible.

30
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:14,875
Use Usage Explorer to trace a headline to approved source records without assuming intent.

31
00:02:14,876 --> 00:02:18,546
Missing optional data means unavailable, not zero activity.

32
00:02:18,547 --> 00:02:22,946
This is decision support, not billing, compliance, or personnel evidence.

33
00:02:23,703 --> 00:02:31,389
That is Cowork Adoption Intelligence: one testing template for reach, return, workflow maturity, champions, and transparent modeled value.

34
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:37,746
Start with the fabricated sample, review the definitions, then connect approved exports to build an evidence-aware enablement plan.
